Someone may find a Hearse transported bones file for the Temple of
Nalzok,  the Priest Quest locate level, containing a corpse formerly
the Glory of Antioch named Rodney (potential for misunderstanding
there). He was killed by Nalzok whilst pursued by many undead. The kit
will include:

+7 Stormbringer
Amulet of Reflection
Rings of Regeneration, Invisibility
Cloak of Displacement
Red Dragon Scales (not mail)
+1 Gauntlets of Power
Two bags of holding
Luckstone

Dwarvish Mithril suits (X2), Robe and +5 Dwarvish roundshield were
lost during the Quest. Intrinsic AC of 1. Max luck. Low Int, high
everything else. Level 17 IIRC - wraith corpses and affectionate
succubi helped in the Quest.

Inside one of the BoHs, the following somewhat embarrassing items will
be found:

Amulet of Lifesaving
Amulet of Lifesaving [sic]
Ring of Conflict
7 or 8 Scrolls of Teleport

/me needed to think a little longer and a little harder before
ascending the staircase to the Temple.

There will also be a statue of a Stone Golem named Horace, who sadly
couldn't withstand wraiths' level drain attacks. He started out as a
blessed figurine of a straw golem, before Rodney slapped him with a
cockatrice corpse and zapped him with wands of speed monster and make
invisible. Horace slew all shopkeepers Rodney met (except Izchak) and
the (coaligned) Priest in the Mine Town, who was then sacrificed upon
his own altar. Surely that should have annoyed Mars?

Chaotic priests seem to get a rough deal on the Quest. Almost all
monsters therein (excepting afformentioned Mindflayer, Red  Dragon
summoned by Nalzok) are level drain resistant, although Stormbringer's
level drain resistance was certainly useful. Lawfuls get Excalibur,
and Neutrals may get Mojo at Expert skill. Not fair I say...


